course: dictionary
lesson: 179
title: The word ahem
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ahem is a small sound, written down as a word. People make it with a little cough to get attention, or to show they are about to speak. In the story, «The Mouse says "Ahem!" before he starts talking» is a clear example.
explain: Ahem can also show that you do not approve of something. When a teacher says «Ahem» to a noisy class, she is hinting that she wants quiet. Read the words around it to work out which meaning fits.
explain: The second meaning is for fun. «My birthday is next week, ahem.» The writer is not coughing at all. They are dropping a hint, and joking that they hope you remember.
fact: Ahem is a written sound, like a small cough.
fact: «Ahem» means a cough to get people's attention, or to show you are about to speak.
fact: «Ahem» can also show that you do not approve of something.
fact: In a humorous use, «ahem» points out a joke or a hint.
fact: In «Alice's Adventures in Wonderland», the Mouse says «Ahem!» before a dull history lesson, to sound important.
exercise: «The children went quiet when the teacher said ahem.» Why did the teacher say ahem? | *To get the class's attention | To say she was hungry | To tell a joke | To start a song
exercise: «My birthday is next week, ahem.» What is the writer doing? | Asking for a glass of water | Coughing because they are ill | Singing a song | *Dropping a hint, as a joke
exercise: Ahem is a sound written as a word. Which word group does it belong to? | Verb | Adjective | *Interjection | Noun
test: In the story, the Mouse says «Ahem!» before a dull lesson. What is he trying to do? | Go to sleep | *Sound important and get attention | Sing a song | Dry off after the sea
test: What does a teacher saying «Ahem» to a noisy class show? | She is about to sing | She is very pleased with the class | *She disapproves and wants quiet | She is hungry
exam: Which best describes ahem? | *An interjection, a sound-word used to get attention or to hint | A verb meaning to sing loudly | A noun for a big cat | A place in a castle
